    <div class="blog-content">
      <section>
        <h2>Zanzibar Packing Essentials (All Seasons)</h2>
        <p>These items are non-negotiable regardless of when you visit:</p>
        
        <h3>Documents & Money</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Passport (valid 6+ months) + photocopies/digital backup</li>
          <li>Tanzania e-Visa approval (printed + digital)</li>
          <li>Travel insurance documents</li>
          <li>Yellow fever certificate (if required)</li>
          <li>USD cash (clean, post-2013 series) + credit cards</li>
          <li>Emergency contact list + Spice & Sail WhatsApp: +255 672 450 934</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Health & Toiletries</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Reef-safe sunscreen (SPF 50+) — <strong>mandatory for marine parks</strong></li>
          <li>Insect repellent (DEET 30-50% or picaridin)</li>
          <li>Antimalarials (consult your doctor; Malarone/Doxycycline common)</li>
          <li>Oral rehydration salts / electrolyte packets</li>
          <li>Basic first aid: plasters, antiseptic wipes, antihistamine, ibuprofen</li>
          <li>Prescription meds + copies of prescriptions</li>
          <li>Hand sanitizer + wet wipes</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Tech & Electronics</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Universal travel adapter (Type G / UK 3-pin for Tanzania)</li>
          <li>Power bank (20,000mAh+ for long boat days)</li>
          <li>Phone + offline maps (Maps.me, Organic Maps)</li>
          <li>Camera + underwater housing/GoPro for snorkeling</li>
          <li>Spare SD cards + portable SSD for backups</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Seasonal Packing Guides</h2>
        
        <h3>☀️ Dry Season (Jun–Oct) — Peak Season</h3>
        <p><strong>Weather:</strong> 24–30°C, low humidity, consistent breeze, minimal rain</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Light, breathable layers (cotton/linen)</li>
          <li>Light fleece or cardigan for early morning boat departures</li>
          <li>Wide-brim hat + polarized sunglasses</li>
          <li>Light rain jacket (just in case)</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>🌧️ Green Season (Mar–May) — Long Rains</h3>
        <p><strong>Weather:</strong> 25–31°C, high humidity, daily afternoon downpours</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Quick-dry clothing (avoid heavy cotton/denim)</li>
          <li>Quality waterproof jacket + pack cover</li>
          <li>Waterproof sandals / quick-dry shoes</li>
          <li>Dry bags for electronics + documents</li>
          <li>Anti-fungal powder (humidity)</li>
          <li>Light long sleeves for mosquito protection</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>🌤️ Shoulder Season (Nov–Dec) — Short Rains</h3>
        <p><strong>Weather:</strong> 26–32°C, brief showers, mostly sunny</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Mix of dry + green season items</li>
          <li>Light rain jacket essential</li>
          <li>Quick-dry everything</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>🎄 Festive Season (Dec 20–Jan 7)</h3>
        <p><strong>Weather:</strong> Hot, humid, occasional showers, busy</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Festive outfit for Christmas/New Year dinners</li>
          <li>Extra sunscreen (strong UV)</li>
          <li>Book activities early — limited availability</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Activity-Specific Packing</h2>
        
        <h3>🏝️ Beach & Snorkeling</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>2–3 swimsuits (rotate for drying)</li>
          <li>Rash guard / UV shirt (essential for snorkeling)</li>
          <li>Reef-safe sunscreen (SPF 50, no oxybenzone/octinoxate)</li>
          <li>Water shoes / reef walkers</li>
          <li>Dry bag for phone/camera on boat</li>
          <li>Microfiber towel (quick-dry, compact)</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>🏄 Kite Surfing (Jun–Sep)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Your own harness (if you have one)</li>
          <li>Board shorts + rash guard</li>
          <li>Wetsuit top (1–2mm) for morning sessions</li>
          <li>Kite repair kit (if bringing own gear)</li>
          <li>Sunglasses with strap (polarized)</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>🦁 Safari (Mikumi, Nyerere, Serengeti)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Neutral colors (khaki, olive, beige) — no bright colors/white</li>
          <li>Long sleeves/pants for sun + insect protection</li>
          <li>Light fleece for early morning game drives</li>
          <li>Closed walking shoes/boots</li>
          <li>Binoculars (8x42 or 10x42)</li>
          <li>Camera with zoom lens (200mm+)</li>
          <li>Headlamp + spare batteries</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>🕌 Stone Town & Cultural Visits</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Modest clothing: shoulders & knees covered</li>
          <li>Light scarf for mosque visits</li>
          <li>Comfortable walking shoes (uneven streets)</li>
          <li>Small day bag for water/souvenirs</li>
          <li>Cash in small denominations (TZS) for markets</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3>🐬 Dolphin Tour (Kizimkazi, 6 AM)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Swimsuit worn under clothes</li>
          <li>Towel + change of clothes for after</li>
          <li>Light jacket for early morning boat</li>
          <li>Seasickness meds if prone</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What NOT to Pack</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>❌ Single-use plastics (banned in Tanzania)</li>
          <li>❌ Non-reef-safe sunscreen (confiscated at marine parks)</li>
          <li>❌ Camouflage/military-style clothing (restricted)</li>
          <li>❌ Drones without permit (strict regulations)</li>
          <li>❌ Heavy denim/jeans (slow to dry, heavy)</li>
          <li>❌ Expensive jewelry (unnecessary risk)</li>
          <li>❌ Sleeping bag (all accommodations provide bedding)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

